+# Similarity report
+
+The 20 regions of our tree closest to the reference (`ab3fe9dffb0a`), ranked by the n-gram score (sum of shared-run lengths over the gate size, for runs within 12 lines of each other on both sides). Written by `python -m tooling.checks similarity --require-ref --closest 20 --report`; a person reads each region and fills in **Verdict** (`independent`, `protocol-mandated`, `convention` or `fix`) and **Note**. A region without a verdict, or marked `fix`, fails the release gate. Not pass/fail by score. Rows are matched across runs by **Key**; edit only the last two columns.
+
+| # | Key | Ours | Reference | Score | Detectors | Excerpt (ours) | Verdict | Note |
